        </Field>
        <Field>
          <Tag>7700</Tag>
          <Name></Name>
          <Required>N</Required>
          <Type>String</Type>
          <Description>Mass Cancel Inst Y At least one character must be provided (PID Filter). Contiguous characters must be specified up to total length. Truncated (unspecified) characters will default to values indicated below. 1st Character : Firm Filter A = No filtering by trading firm is performed. F = All orders that were sent on a port configured with the “” as under the specified Firm Identifier in Sender Comp ID (49). Note only one firm can be killed by a drop port (the Sender Comp ID (49) firm), so this filter is not meaningful and can always be specified as ‘A’). 2nd Character : Acknowledgement Style M = (default) Individual Execution Reports are sent for each cancelled order. S = Single sent Purge Acknowledgement once all cancels have been processed. Single will contain Purge Acknowledgement Mass Cancel Id (7695) and Cancelled Order Count (7696). Mass Cancel Id (7695) must be specified or the will be rejected. Purge Request B = Both individual and Execution Reports single . Also Purge Acknowledgement</Description>
        </Field>
        <Field>
          <Tag>7695</Tag>
          <Name></Name>
          <Required>N</Required>
          <Type>String</Type>
          <Description>Mass Cancel ID N Mass Cancel ID – This field will be echoed back in the resulting when Purge Acknowledgement second character of Mass Cancel Inst (7700) is set to ‘S’ or ‘B’. Purge requests containing a currently outstanding Mass Cancel ID will be rejected. Mass Cancel ID cannot end with a space. Maximum length 20 (extra characters will be ignored).</Description>
        </Field>
        <Field>
          <Tag>55</Tag>
          <Name>Symbol</Name>
          <Required>N</Required>
          <Type>String</Type>
          <Description>Symbol N Symbol (upper case). Limits cancellations to only orders with the specified symbol.</Description>
        </Field>
        <Field>
          <Tag>37</Tag>
          <Name>OrderID</Name>
          <Required>N</Required>
          <Type>String</Type>
          <Description>Order ID N To cancel a single order, enter the Order ID supplied by Cboe on the order acknowledgement. In the case of multiple changes to a single order, this will be the Order Id from the most recent acknowledgement.</Description>
        </Field>
      </Fields>
    </Message>

